  "question": {
    "text": "Let $f(x)=3 x^{10}-7\r\nx^{8}+5 x^{6}-21 x^{3}+3 x^{2}-7$\r\nThen $\\lim _{h \\rightarrow 0} \\frac{f(1-h)-f(1)}{h^{3}+3 h}$"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "does not exist",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "is $\\frac{50}{3}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "is $\\frac{53}{3}$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "is $\\frac{22}{3}$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "We have, $f(x)=3 x^{10}-7 x^{8}+5 x^{6}-21 x^{3}+3 x^{2}-7$\r\n$\\therefore \\quad f(1-h)=3(1-h)^{10}-7(1-h)^{8}$\r\n$+5(1-h)^{6}-21\\left(1-h^{3}+3(1-h)^{2}-7\\right.$\r\n$=3\\left(1-10 h+45 h^{2}-120 h^{3}+\\ldots \\ldots+h^{10}\\right)$\r\n$-7\\left(1-8 h+28 h^{2}-56 h^{3}+\\ldots . .+h^{8}\\right)$\r\n$+5\\left(1-6 h+15 h^{2}-20 h^{3}+\\ldots . .+h^{6}\\right)$\r\n$-21\\left(1-3 h+3 h^{2}-h^{3}\\right)$\r\n$+3\\left(1-2 h+h^{2}\\right)-7$\r\n$\\Rightarrow f(1-h)=-24+53 h+h^{2}(-46)+h^{3}(-47)+\\ldots$\r\nand $\\quad f(1)=-24$\r\n$\\therefore \\quad \\lim _{h \\rightarrow 0} \\frac{f(1-h)-f(1)}{h^{3}+3 h}$\r\n$=\\lim _{h \\rightarrow 0} \\frac{-24+53 h+h^{2}(-46)+h^{3}(-47)+\\ldots-(-24)}{h\\left(h^{2}+3\\right)}$\r\n$=\\lim _{h \\rightarrow 0} \\frac{53 h+h^{2}(-46)+h^{3}(-47)+\\ldots}{h\\left(h^{2}+3\\right)}$\r\n$=\\lim _{h \\rightarrow 0} \\frac{53+h(-46)+h^{2}(-47)+\\ldots}{h^{2}+3}=\\frac{53}{3}$"
  }
}